```verilog
output Q0, Q1, Q2, Q3;
input D, S1, S0;
```

The module should route the data input `D` to one of the four outputs (`Q0`, `Q1`, `Q2`, `Q3`) based on the 2-bit select input formed by `S1` (most significant bit) and `S0` (least significant bit). Specifically, when the select input `S1S0` is `00`, `D` should be routed to `Q0`; when `S1S0` is `01`, `D` should be routed to `Q1`; when `S1S0` is `10`, `D` should be routed to `Q2`; and when `S1S0` is `11`, `D` should be routed to `Q3`. All outputs that are not selected should be driven to logic 0.

